# Push After Testing

When the user asks to **push after testing** (or similar), complete **all** steps below and report results **before** `git push`. Do not push until every gate passes or the user explicitly accepts a documented exception.

## 1. Vercel / deploy readiness

- Run local `npm run build` (must exit 0).
- After push (if user already asked to push), verify GitHub commit status for Vercel: **success**, not pending/failure.
- If Vercel failed, inspect logs, fix root cause, re-test, and push a fix — do not leave main in a failed deploy state without telling the user.

## 2. Accessibility

- Smoke-test key routes locally (home, shop, one CMS page, admin login if applicable).
- Run Lighthouse **accessibility** (target score ≥ 90) or equivalent axe check on the homepage.
- Fix critical a11y regressions (missing alt, broken landmarks, contrast, focus) before push.

## 3. Local without errors

- `npx tsc --noEmit` — no type errors.
- `npm run lint` — no new errors (pre-existing warnings OK if unchanged).
- Dev server starts cleanly: `npm run dev` on port 3010, no crash on load.
- Hit `/` and one admin route; confirm no runtime errors in terminal.

## 4. Performance / Lighthouse

- Run Lighthouse **performance** on local production build (`npm run start` after build) or dev, target score ≥ 80 on homepage.
- Note LCP, CLS, and any failing audits; fix obvious regressions introduced by the change.

## Report format (required)

Before pushing, summarize:

```
Pre-push checklist
- Build: pass/fail
- tsc/lint: pass/fail
- Dev server: pass/fail
- Lighthouse perf: XX (homepage)
- Lighthouse a11y: XX (homepage)
- Vercel: N/A until after push, then re-check
```

After push, re-check Vercel status and report final deploy state.
